  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For 1 - 3, determine whether each ordered pair is a solution to the inequality \(y &gt; x − 1\).</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="53930592-06c9-42dd-b3c1-80d86acbb55b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4f57fb23-4a13-46c7-bade-4751d590d15b" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((0,1)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2e0361f0-9152-4dfd-91ed-b78c12827035" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\((−4,−1)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b0de4861-3d99-462f-b776-39e212e0fc77" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((4,2)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revist activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <para>For 4 - 6, determine whether each ordered pair is a solution to the inequality \(y &gt; x − 3\).</para>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7b40b269-3d20-4270-a430-706c08eb23ab" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((0,0)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes, \((0,0)\) is a solution to the inequality.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Remember to substitute the coordinates into the inequality to check if it holds true.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1fc70666-6c63-4cc0-8df5-53817254d3b5" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((2,1)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No, \((2,1)\) is not a solution to the inequality.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Check the inequality with the given coordinates.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6a8c18e6-92fc-43ad-ba1e-d1351ac96415" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((−1,−5)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <para>For questions 7 and 8, determine whether each ordered pair is a solution to the inequality \(2x + 3y &gt; 2.\)</para>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f12e8b48-6d40-47d3-ae44-2f85f62d6c21" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((1,1)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2c7ac670-7c24-412c-ade2-c8818efc0611" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \((4,−3)\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
