  <!--Q12-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04793c5c-6570-44f1-9a26-ee459ae51b57" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((3, 7)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((1, 5)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((3, 7)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((5, 11)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-3, -1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Consider the linear equation \(2y − 3x = 5\). The pair \((-1,1)\) is a solution to the equation. Which of
          the following is also a solution to the equation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (3, 7)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.11.2. </para>
