    <problem>
      <para>The boundary line on the graph represents the equation \( 5x + 2y = 6\). Write an inequality that is represented by the graph.</para>
      <figure><media alt="graph with boundary line that represents the equation 5x + 2y = 6"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a9a4189f06a5a2df644f610859ad8385a70f7031"/></media></figure></problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(5x + 2y &lt; 6\)</para>
    </solution>
